M1c.\u0275cmp=t({type:M1c,selectors:[["enable-analytics-page"]],inputs:{initialValue:"initialValue",isImportingCloudProject:"isImportingCloudProject"},outputs:{prev:"prev",next:"next"},decls:74,vars:27,consts:()=>[["abtPopover",""],["targetingPopover",""],["crashalyticsPopover",""],["cloudFunctionsPopover",""],["reportingPopover",""]," Google Analytics\ufffd#4\ufffd\ufffd/#4\ufffd for your Firebase project "," Google Analytics is a free and unlimited analytics solution that enables targeting, reporting, and more in Firebase Crashlytics, Cloud Messaging, In-App Messaging, Remote Config, A/B Testing, and Cloud Functions. ",
" Google Analytics enables: "," A/B testing"," Firebase A/B Testing allows you to experiment with app behavior or different text for Cloud Messaging notifications sent to users. A/B Testing requires Google Analytics. "," User segmentation & targeting across Firebase products"," Firebase Cloud Messaging, Remote Config, In-App Messaging, and other products rely on Google Analytics for results measurement and most targeting options. "," Breadcrumb logs in Crashlytics"," Breadcrumb logs are created from Google Analytics events. Firebase Crashlytics uses breadcrumb logs to help provide information about a session leading up to the crash, non-fatal, or ANR event. ",
" Event-based Cloud Functions triggers"," Analytics allows you to trigger a Cloud Function when users perform a specific action (an Analytics event) in your app. "," Free unlimited reporting"," Google Analytics includes free, unlimited analytics reporting for up to 500 distinct event types, along with a robust dashboard and reporting tools available right in the Firebase console. "," Enable Google Analytics for this project "," Recommended "," Previous "," Create project "," Add Firebase "," Continue ",
